--- collections — collection types for the handl runtime.
---
--- This is an aggregator crate: it bundles many collection modules
--- (vec, list, queue, stack, deque, hash_map, hash_set, array, btree_map,
--- btree_set, priority_queue, bit_set). The Rust Module/Function impls live
--- in plugin-lib-collections; this .hnl file declares the aggregated
--- interface surface (capabilities) for the plugin system.
---
--- The btree_map, btree_set, priority_queue, and bit_set modules are
--- reserved for future implementation.
---
--- ## vec module
--- vec.new — create a new empty vec (back-ended dynamic array).
--- vec.from — create a vec from an existing array.
--- vec.to_array — return the vec as a plain array.
--- vec.len — return the number of elements in a vec.
--- vec.is_empty — test whether a vec is empty.
--- vec.push — push a value onto the back of a vec.
--- vec.pop — remove and return the value at the back of a vec.
--- vec.peek — return the value at the back of a vec without removing it.
---
--- ## list module
--- list.new — create a new empty list (front-ended list).
--- list.from — create a list from an existing array.
--- list.to_array — return the list as a plain array.
--- list.len — return the number of elements in a list.
--- list.is_empty — test whether a list is empty.
--- list.push — push a value onto the front of a list.
--- list.pop — remove and return the value at the front of a list.
--- list.peek — return the value at the front of a list without removing it.
---
--- ## queue module
--- queue.new — create a new empty FIFO queue.
--- queue.from — create a queue from an existing array.
--- queue.to_array — return the queue as a plain array.
--- queue.len — return the number of elements in a queue.
--- queue.is_empty — test whether a queue is empty.
--- queue.enqueue — add a value to the back of a queue.
--- queue.dequeue — remove and return the value at the front of a queue.
--- queue.peek — return the value at the front of a queue without removing it.
---
--- ## stack module
--- stack.new — create a new empty LIFO stack.
--- stack.from — create a stack from an existing array.
--- stack.to_array — return the stack as a plain array.
--- stack.len — return the number of elements in a stack.
--- stack.is_empty — test whether a stack is empty.
--- stack.push — push a value onto the top (back) of a stack.
--- stack.pop — remove and return the value at the top (back) of a stack.
--- stack.peek — return the value at the top (back) of a stack without removing it.
---
--- ## deque module
--- deque.new — create a new empty double-ended queue.
--- deque.from — create a deque from an existing array.
--- deque.to_array — return the deque as a plain array.
--- deque.len — return the number of elements in a deque.
--- deque.is_empty — test whether a deque is empty.
--- deque.push_back — push a value onto the back of a deque.
--- deque.push_front — push a value onto the front of a deque.
--- deque.pop_back — remove and return the value at the back of a deque.
--- deque.pop_front — remove and return the value at the front of a deque.
--- deque.peek_back — return the value at the back of a deque without removing it.
--- deque.peek_front — return the value at the front of a deque without removing it.
---
--- ## hash_map module
--- hash_map.new — create a new empty hash map (key/value dictionary).
--- hash_map.from — create a hash map from an existing object.
--- hash_map.to_object — return the hash map as a plain object.
--- hash_map.len — return the number of entries in a hash map.
--- hash_map.is_empty — test whether a hash map is empty.
--- hash_map.get — get the value for a key, with an optional default.
--- hash_map.set — set a key/value pair in a hash map, returning a new map.
--- hash_map.remove — remove a key from a hash map, returning a new map.
--- hash_map.has — test whether a hash map contains a key.
--- hash_map.keys — return the keys of a hash map as an array.
--- hash_map.values — return the values of a hash map as an array.
--- hash_map.entries — return the entries of a hash map as an array of [key, value] pairs.
--- hash_map.size — return the number of entries in a hash map (alias of len).
--- hash_map.get_or — get the value for a key, returning a default if null or missing.
--- hash_map.deep_get — get a value at a dot-separated path in a nested object.
--- hash_map.path_or — get a value at a dot-separated path, returning a default if not found.
--- hash_map.update — update a key's value via a function, returning a new map.
--- hash_map.set_path — set a value at a dot-separated path, returning a new object.
--- hash_map.update_path — update a value at a dot-separated path via a function.
--- hash_map.map_values — transform each value in a hash map via a function.
--- hash_map.map_keys — transform each key in a hash map via a function.
--- hash_map.filter_keys — filter a hash map by a predicate on keys.
--- hash_map.filter_values — filter a hash map by a predicate on values.
--- hash_map.invert — swap keys and values in a hash map.
--- hash_map.clone_deep — deep-clone a value.
--- hash_map.pick — select a subset of keys from a hash map.
--- hash_map.omit — exclude a subset of keys from a hash map.
--- hash_map.merge — merge two hash maps (second overwrites first).
--- hash_map.deep_merge — recursively merge two hash maps.
--- hash_map.from_entries — construct a hash map from an array of [key, value] pairs.
--- hash_map.has_key — test whether a hash map contains a key (alias of has).
---
--- ## hash_set module
--- hash_set.new — create a new empty hash set (unordered set of unique values).
--- hash_set.from — create a hash set from an existing array (deduplicated).
--- hash_set.to_array — return the hash set as a plain array.
--- hash_set.len — return the number of values in a hash set.
--- hash_set.is_empty — test whether a hash set is empty.
--- hash_set.add — add a value to a hash set, returning a new set.
--- hash_set.remove — remove a value from a hash set, returning a new set.
--- hash_set.has — test whether a hash set contains a value.
--- hash_set.union — return the union of two sets.
--- hash_set.intersection — return the intersection of two sets.
--- hash_set.difference — return the difference of two sets (a minus b).
--- hash_set.unique — deduplicate an array, preserving first-occurrence order.
--- hash_set.symmetric_difference — return elements in exactly one of two sets.
--- hash_set.without — remove specified values from an array (deduplicated).
--- hash_set.unique_by — deduplicate an array by a key function.
---
--- ## array module
--- array.len — return the length of an array.
--- array.reverse — reverse the elements of an array.
--- array.concat — concatenate two arrays.
--- array.contains — test whether an array contains a value.
--- array.index_of — return the index of the first occurrence of a value, or -1.
--- array.slice — slice an array by start and end indices.
--- array.first — return the first element of an array, or null if empty.
--- array.last — return the last element of an array, or null if empty.
--- array.at — return the element at a given index, or null if out of bounds.
--- array.push — append one or more values to the end of an array.
--- array.pop — remove the last element from an array.
--- array.shift — remove the first element from an array.
--- array.fill — create an array of n copies of a value.
--- array.flatten — flatten one level of nesting in an array.
--- array.deep_flatten — recursively flatten all nesting in an array.
--- array.take — take the first n elements of an array.
--- array.drop — drop the first n elements of an array.
--- array.enumerate — pair each element with its index as [index, value].
--- array.unzip — split an array of pairs into two arrays.
--- array.intersperse — insert a separator between each element of an array.
--- array.intercalate — insert a separator array between each sub-array of an array.
--- array.dedupe — remove consecutive duplicate elements from an array.
--- array.prepend — prepend a value to the beginning of an array.
--- array.take_while — take elements while a predicate holds.
--- array.drop_while — drop elements while a predicate holds.
--- array.scan — leftward scan with a function and initial accumulator.
--- array.foldr — rightward fold with a function and initial accumulator.
--- array.find_index — return the index of the first element matching a predicate, or -1.
--- array.find_last — return the last element matching a predicate, or null.
--- array.find_last_index — return the index of the last element matching a predicate, or -1.
--- array.windows — return sliding windows of a given size over an array.
--- array.transpose — transpose rows to columns in a 2D array.
--- array.insert_at — insert a value at a given index in an array.
--- array.remove_at — remove the element at a given index from an array.
--- array.range — generate a range of numbers from start to end with an optional step.
--- array.zip — zip two arrays into an array of pairs.
--- array.chunk — split an array into chunks of a given size.
--- array.compact — remove null values from an array.
--- array.pluck — extract a named key from each object in an array.
---
--- ## btree_map module (reserved)
--- btree_map — ordered key/value dictionary backed by a B-tree (reserved for future implementation).
---
--- ## btree_set module (reserved)
--- btree_set — ordered set of unique values (reserved for future implementation).
---
--- ## priority_queue module (reserved)
--- priority_queue — priority queue / heap (reserved for future implementation).
---
--- ## bit_set module (reserved)
--- bit_set — compact set of non-negative integers stored as bits (reserved for future implementation).
